  "brief": "Altria is considering a takeover bid for Imperial Brands, the parent company of Nobel and Fortuna, in a deal still in its early stages.\n\nAltria / Imperial Brands (Rumored): Altria to Acquire Imperial Brands. Altria is considering a takeover bid for Imperial Brands, the parent company of Nobel and Fortuna [4, 5, 8]. The deal is still in its early stages, with no official announcement made yet [1, 2, 3]. Japan Tobacco is also reportedly eyeing a deal with Imperial Brands [5, 8]. The future of the deal is uncertain at this point [6, 7].\nExpedia Group / Kiwi.com (Announced): Expedia Group Acquires Kiwi.com. Expedia Group is acquiring Kiwi.com to expand its European flight business [14, 13, 12]. The deal was announced on November 25, 2023 [14, 13, 12]. The acquisition is expected to augment Expedia's flights capabilities [14, 13, 12].\nTarga Resources / Kinetik (Rumored): Targa Resources and Kinetik Deal Rumors. Targa Resources is reportedly eyeing Kinetik as data centers drive gas demand [15, 16, 17]. Targa Resources is in talks to acquire Kinetik, according to Bloomberg reports [16, 17, 19]. Kinetik's stock price jumped on the news of Targa Resources' interest in acquiring the company [18].\nLS Power / Constellation (Completed): LS Power Acquires Constellation Assets. LS Power has acquired 4.4 GW natural gas generation assets from Constellation [20, 21]. The deal is now completed [20, 21].\nRottenstone Gold Inc. / Great Bear Royalty (Announced): Rottenstone Gold Inc. Acquires Great Bear Royalty. Rottenstone Gold Inc. is acquiring Great Bear Royalty [22]. The deal was announced [22]. No further information is available [22].\nIntegral / I-ne (Announced): Integral to Acquire I-ne. Integral is acquiring I-ne, a maker of BOTANIST, in a $110M deal [23].\nUmios / High Liner Foods (Announced): Umios to Acquire High Liner Foods. Umios is acquiring High Liner Foods for C$27.00 per share [24, 25]. The deal has been endorsed by ISS and Glass Lewis [24]. A special meeting of shareholders is scheduled for December 15 [25].\nSpaceX / Tesla (Pending approval): SpaceX and Tesla in Talks. SpaceX and Tesla are in talks for a $3.5 trillion merger [26, 27, 28]. The deal is still pending approval [26, 27, 28]. No new information is available [29, 30, 31].\n\nAlso worth knowing:\n- FutureMain signs SPAC deal for Nasdaq listing in 2027 [32].\n- FutureMain Sets Its Sights on Nasdaq, Bringing Decades of Industrial Expertise Into the AI Era [33].\n- United Polyfab to convert 2.29 crore warrants at ₹18.89 on Nov 30 [34].",
